==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
{{compound|hard|wood}}
===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{context|countable|lang=en}} (mostly in botany and forestry) The [[wood]] from any [[dicotyledon]]ous tree, without regard to its hardness.
#: {{usex|Balsa is a '''hardwood''', but a soft hardwood.|lang=en}}
# {{context|countable|lang=en}} (in more general use) As the preceding but limited to those that are commercial [[timber]]s, and are at least average in hardness.
#: {{usex|Ash, hickory and oak are some of the most prominent domestic '''hardwoods'''.|lang=en}}
# {{context|countable|forestry|lang=en}} The tree or tree species that yields the preceding.
#: {{usex|This '''hardwood''' has been planted extensively throughout the hills here.|lang=en}}
# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} A joint term for the commercial timbers, without distinguishing which.
#: {{usex|You should have used '''hardwood''' for this window sill instead of this junk.|lang=en}}
# {{context|sports|slang|lang=en}} The sport of basketball, in particular the basketball court.

